# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit it.
# Read by scripts/factory-secrets.sh, which copies these values out into
# every new project's own GitHub Actions secrets — this file isn't
# ai-app-factory's own config so much as a personal, reusable staging area
# for provisioning *other* repos. See DESIGN.md's "GH_PAT: token strategy"
# and docs/adr/0001-design-to-issues-loop.md for the full picture.

# From `claude setup-token` (Claude Code OAuth, not an API key — see
# README.md's Setup section for why: this authenticates against your Claude
# subscription, not pay-per-token billing). Copied verbatim into every new
# project's own CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN secret.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# A fine-grained GitHub PAT scoped to "All repositories" with ONLY
# `Secrets: Read and write` — nothing else. This value only ever gets used
# for `gh secret set` calls (factory-secrets.sh's entire job), so it needs
# no Contents, Issues, Pull requests, or Administration permission at all.
# "All repositories" is unavoidable here specifically (not a shortcut): this
# same value seeds every future project's own GH_PAT before that project's
# repo exists, so a selected-repos token structurally can't cover it yet —
# same reasoning ai-app-factory's own (much more narrowly-scoped) GH_PAT
# avoided by not needing repo-creation rights at all. This one's blast
# radius stays small by *capability* (can only ever write new secret
# values, never read code or open anything) rather than by repo coverage.
GH_PAT=
